# [Personal Messages](messages)

Mail the crew get while they fly. One heading per message.

**This file is meant to be added to.** You do not need to read any code to write one -
copy a message below, change the words. The rules are short:

- `From:` is who it is from, and a message without one is ignored. Write it the way it
  would show on a phone: `Your sister, Mira`, not `mira_01`.
- `To:` is a console - `helm`, `weapons`, `engineering`, `science`, `comms`, `hangar` -
  or a comma list, or `*` for the whole crew. Leave it out and everyone gets it.
- A line like `- [Say this](anything) ; signal something_happened` is a REPLY the crew
  can send back. Up to four per message; leave them out for a message that is just
  telling them something. The `; signal name` part is optional and lets the mission
  react - ask whoever wired the mission what to put there, or leave it off.
- `After:` is how many seconds into the mission it arrives. Leave it out and it is
  waiting when they sit down. Spread them out; mail that all lands at once is a
  document, not a message.
- The heading is the subject line. The paragraph under the fence is the message.
- Keep it under about 600 characters and keep it ASCII - the engine draws no curly
  quotes, no em-dashes and no emoji, and a `^` is a line break to it.

Do NOT add a `Kind:` field. It means something else in AMD and will quietly break the
records under it.


## [Did you take the good pan](mail_pan)
---
From: Your flatmate, Devi
To: engineering
---
The good pan is missing. Your bunk is missing. I have connected these two facts. If
the pan is on a starship somewhere past Jupiter I would like it noted that I have not
called anybody about it, which I think makes me a very good flatmate. Bring it back.


## [Nan says hello](mail_nan)
---
From: Mum
After: 90
---
Your nan has learned what a subspace relay is and now believes she can be heard by
everyone on the ship at once, so she has started saying hello to all of them. Hello to
the pilot. Hello to whoever does the guns. She has been at this for an hour. Please eat
something green.


## [The cat has opinions](mail_cat)
---
From: Sam
To: helm
After: 200
---
Update on the cat: still furious. Sits on your chair. Not near your chair, ON it, in
the exact middle, staring at the door like a small landlord waiting on rent. I told her
you were saving the frontier. She was unmoved. Fly safe. Come home.


## [Re: your expenses claim](mail_expenses)
---
From: Fleet Accounts (do not reply)
After: 320
---
Claim TSN-4471 has been returned. Line item "one (1) planet, incidental" has been
queried. Accounts understands that the planet was already there and that you did not
purchase it. Accounts requires a receipt regardless. Please resubmit within thirty
days.


## [I have your plant](mail_plant)
---
From: Your neighbour, Ade
To: science
After: 420
---
The plant is alive. I want that on record first because of what comes next. It has
grown a second thing. Not a leaf. A THING. It is facing the window. It was not facing
the window on Tuesday. You said it was a fern. Ade.


## [From the yard](mail_yard)
---
From: Chief Petty Officer Anwar, TSN Dockyard
To: engineering
After: 540
---
Whoever signed off the coolant loop on your hull did it at 0400 and it shows. The
second manifold is a repair, not a part. She will hold. She will also make a noise
about it and you will think something has gone wrong, and nothing will have gone wrong.
That is just her telling you she remembers.


## [Small emergency, resolved](mail_kid)
---
From: Jo
After: 700
---
Your godson told his whole class that you fight space monsters for a living. His
teacher rang to check. I said yes. I did not know what else to say and, on reflection,
it is not even a lie, is it. He would like a photograph of a monster. Not a scary one.


## [You left this on](mail_oven)
---
From: Your flatmate, Devi
After: 880
---
Second message because I have found the pan. It was in the oven. The oven was on. It
has been on since you left. I am no longer a very good flatmate, I am a person who
lives alone in a warm flat with one ruined pan, and I would like you to know that the
frontier is not the only place where things are difficult.


## [Are you eating](mail_eating)
---
From: Mum
After: 150
---
Do not just say yes. Your nan wants to know what, specifically, and she will be able to
tell if you are making it up.

- [Tell her the truth](truth) ; signal mail_ate_badly
- [Make something up](lie) ; signal mail_lied_to_nan
- [Say the replicator is broken](dodge)


## [The pan, a negotiation](mail_pan_deal)
---
From: Your flatmate, Devi
To: engineering
After: 620
---
I have priced a replacement pan. I am prepared to be reasonable about this, which is
more than you deserve, and I would like you to notice that I am being reasonable.

- [Offer to pay for it](pay) ; signal mail_pan_paid
- [Point out it was in the oven](blame) ; signal mail_pan_blamed
- [Send a photograph of a nebula instead](deflect)


## [Sector control, routine](mail_control)
---
From: TSN Sector Control
After: 480
---
Routine check. Your transponder has been reading intermittently for six hours. Confirm
your status so we can close the log, or declare and we will send somebody.

- [All well, closing the log](fine) ; signal mail_control_fine
- [Declare a fault](fault) ; signal mail_control_fault
